      "task": "Construct the entire graph of 2x+3y=12 and determine which quadrant contains none of its points.",
      "independent_solution": {
        "task_id_graph": "547-graph",
        "algebra": "3y=12-2x, so y=4-(2/3)x, for every real x. Conversely, substituting this y gives 2x+3y=12, so this describes the entire solution set.",
        "graph_set": "{(x, 4-(2/3)x): x is real}",
        "construction": "Plot the y-intercept (0,4) and the x-intercept (6,0), then extend their straight line without endpoints in both directions. The slope is (0-4)/(6-0)=-2/3.",
        "decisive_points": [
          {"x": -3, "y": 6, "role": "quadrant II witness", "substitution": "2*(-3)+3*6=-6+18=12"},
          {"x": 0, "y": 4, "role": "y-axis intercept", "substitution": "2*0+3*4=12"},
          {"x": 3, "y": 2, "role": "quadrant I witness", "substitution": "2*3+3*2=6+6=12"},
          {"x": 6, "y": 0, "role": "x-axis intercept", "substitution": "2*6+3*0=12"},
